    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "Thanks for the list. One thing is bothering me though—the refrigeration unit didn't just lose power, it actually seemed to short-circuit right after a series of small, weird mechanical clicking sounds. It doesn't make sense because the maintenance logs say the unit was brand new. Do you think this could be a hardware defect or maybe some kind of systemic failure in the electrical components? I'm trying to figure out if this was a freak accident or if there's an underlying issue we missed.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
