      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Firstly, let's attempt to systematically determine the cause of the refrigeration unit failure. Post-initial response, begin an Root Cause Analysis (RCA):\n\n1. Engage a team with electrical and mechanical engineering expertise to examine the refrigeration unit and associated transport systems.\n\n2. Retain a portion of the seafood for detailed microbiological testing to assess immediate spoilage.\n\n3. Perform a thorough electrical diagnostics of the refrigeration system, considering:\n\n   a. Re-conduct electrical history to ensure proper documentation practices, as well as tests for any shorts, overloads, or lack of cooling system indicators like fans.\n\n   b. Cross-check against production and incident reports to identify if any similar malfunctions have been reported previously.\n\n   c. Examine the refrigeration unit for potential hardware defects using a non-destructive testing (NDT) approach, including ultrasonic testing for internal damage and visual inspection for obvious defects.\n\n4. Review maintenance logs and compare equipment histories with the specifications to pinpoint discrepancies.\n\n5. Interview staff and technicians for insights into routine maintenance routines and any recent anomalies.\n\n6. Investigate the possibility of a latent failure of components using data on design life expectancy and known failure rates from similar units or industry standards.\n\n7. In parallel, consult a third-party forensic electrical engineer",
